%N A363999 Numbers of the form |2^i - 3^j|, for i >= 1, j >= 1.
%C A363999 The terms up to A014121(3000) = 328256967394000206715, a(1)..a(2891), are proved by the congruence sieve described in A014121, and formally verified in Lean 4 (see link). - _Ruud H.G. van Tol_, Nov 10 2026
%H A363999 Ruud H.G. van Tol, <a href="/A363999/b363999.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..2891</a>
%H A363999 Ruud H.G. van Tol, <a href="https://github.com/druud/Collatz-but-stop-at-the-drop/blob/main/src/lean_files/AcceleratedCollatz/PowDiff.lean">Lean 4 proof of a(1..2891) and of A014121(1..3000)</a>, 2026.
%o A363999 (PARI) upto(N) = if(N > 328256967394000206715, error("upto: N beyond the proved range")); my(S=List()); for(i=1, 70, for(j=1, 45, my(v=abs(2^i-3^j)); if(v <= N, listput(~S, v)))); Set(S); \\ _Ruud H.G. van Tol_, Nov 10 2026
